--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

None. The application is a single HTML file built from the sources in this
repository: HTML and CSS written for this project, a translation table with
four locales, and about 800 lines of plain JavaScript. It bundles no library,
no framework, no analytics and no font file, and it loads nothing from the
network at runtime - not even a CDN copy of anything.

The ZIP writer (store-only, CRC-32, local headers, central directory and end
of central directory record) is implemented in this project from the public
ZIP file format description. It does not include code from Info-ZIP, zlib,
JSZip or any other ZIP implementation.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
External services
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

None. Images are decoded, resized and re-encoded inside the browser, and the
result is handed to the download manager of the browser. No image, no
filename and no metadata ever leaves the device, which also means the app has
no server-side limits: the only limits are the memory of the browser and the
format support of its own codecs.
